ng edged out as progressives gain ground in primaries through groups like the DSA. Others clarified historical corporatism as state-mediated group negotiations, while modern usage critiques business sway over policy, highlighting ongoing tensions in party language and direction.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T00:11:13.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108347888875307202"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108506324896276883"},{"post_id":"2108532233409867868"},{"post_id":"2108554695694516459"},{"post_id":"2108507450303488153"},{"post_id":"2108547981154947244"},{"post_id":"2108578458771108111"},{"post_id":"2108549148693893297"},{"post_id":"2108554343318471055"},{"post_id":"2108520299650245082"},{"post_id":"2108556464680005827"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108557309890953414","name":"Pallavi Ghosh questions Common Justice Party's shift from student issues to Congress-aligned topics","summary":"Pallavi Ghosh posted on X questioning why the Common Justice Party (CJP), initially formed for student issues, is now addressing topics typically raised by Congress. Discussions accuse CJP of acting as a B-team for Congress, AAP, or BJP to undermine opposition ahead of elections. The post references #VoteChori, electoral roll deletions affecting 13 crore voters, and CJP protests over election irregularities originating from student concerns.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T18:22:55.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108557309890953414"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108535781375819939"},{"post_id":"2108531262797316338"},{"post_id":"2108561256496181392"},{"post_id":"2108586423972491397"},{"post_id":"2108455151744741492"},{"post_id":"2108575697870651502"},{"post_id":"2108583013500268607"},{"post_id":"2108532014945091614"},{"post_id":"2108548224038678762"},{"post_id":"2108516741710225512"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108535453083427289","name":"Green Party of England and Wales Faces Internal Challenges with Deputy Leader Zak Polanski's Position Weakened","summary":"The Green Party of England and Wales is experiencing internal turmoil, with Deputy Leader Zak Polanski's position weakened amid claims of an Islamist faction gaining control through new members. Discussions reference a satirical 'Animal Liberation Party' narrative involving leadership challenges.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T23:48:10.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108535453083427289"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108199071983034726"},{"post_id":"2108199132280348960"},{"post_id":"2108284141724966988"},{"post_id":"2108365208926249112"},{"post_id":"2108199132280348960"},{"post_id":"2108284141724966988"},{"post_id":"2108199071983034726"},{"post_id":"2108212796106379412"},{"post_id":"2108307799382089767"},{"post_id":"2108370876173615335"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"One user's surprise at Mexico's universal healthcare rollout sparked a detailed rundown of the nation's economic power, scientific achievements, and trailblazing leadership.","id":"2108272048485109994","name":"Mexico Advances Universal Healthcare Amid Pride in Economy and Science","summary":"Mexico is launching the Servicio Universal de Salud (SUS) system, with plans for 12,750 primary care clinics opening in January 2027 across 24 states. These facilities will follow a zero-rejection policy, provide basic medicines, and refer patients as needed, building on prior reforms to ease pressure on existing public health centers. Posts celebrated Mexico's $2 trillion economy as America's top trading partner, President Claudia Sheinbaum's energy engineering doctorate and Nobel panel role, plus contributions to ozone research, birth control, and early color TV—while some noted ongoing challenges like medicine shortages and waits.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T02:50:17.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108272048485109994"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108139413394137414"},{"post_id":"2108297287562592747"},{"post_id":"2108354899415298480"},{"post_id":"2108393725969985817"},{"post_id":"2108297287562592747"},{"post_id":"2108341230023389583"},{"post_id":"2108354899415298480"},{"post_id":"2108393725969985817"},{"post_id":"2108412498462322851"},{"post_id":"2108334971215868069"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"One post questioned why some Americans put the Palestine conflict at the top of their political list, even as gas, housing, and food prices squeeze household budgets.","id":"2108412267721027619","name":"Debate Erupts Over Prioritizing Palestine Amid U.S. Cost of Living Pressures","summary":"Mr. Smith expressed bafflement at the focus on Palestine given domestic challenges like voting concerns and rising costs, a view echoed by Booker G. Washington who wondered about people's daily struggles. Replies countered that U.S. aid to Israel—$25.5 billion since October 2023 plus $3.8 billion annually—diverts funds from public services at home, invoking the 'imperial boomerang' where foreign tactics influence domestic policing. Defenders see moral urgency in overseas suffering as linked to U.S. taxes and priorities, while critics argue it overlooks what citizens can directly affect, highlighting divides on global versus local issues.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:25:15.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108412267721027619"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108528917988753683"},{"post_id":"2108504381775569068"},{"post_id":"2108504571660120246"},{"post_id":"2108514534864666999"},{"post_id":"2108521908434084103"},{"post_id":"2108491671750967485"},{"post_id":"2108513096054800482"},{"post_id":"2108488574165303600"},{"post_id":"2108479591736291573"},{"post_id":"2108544544102899772"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108552286842892409","name":"Nigerians Mock APC Supporters for Protesting on Flooded Road","summary":"Social media users mocked APC supporters for holding a protest on a badly flooded road featuring a large puddle. Critics accused the protesters of being paid small stipends and acting as political jobbers while supporting President Tinubu. Discussions highlighted Nigeria's infrastructure failures.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T13:41:33.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108552286842892409"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108232748318278044"},{"post_id":"2108396164672532585"},{"post_id":"2108398344934699404"},{"post_id":"2108428320484339929"},{"post_id":"2108440661305290958"},{"post_id":"2108391859252781558"},{"post_id":"2108409619106377855"},{"post_id":"2108396164672532585"},{"post_id":"2108428560595616254"},{"post_id":"2108398344934699404"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Milka Nyambura, a nominated MCA in Nyandarua County, paused and hesitated over her notes while questioning a chief officer in an October 2026 session. The moment quickly divided viewers online.","id":"2108447066401939760","name":"Video of Nyandarua MCA's Struggling Question Fuels Debate on Qualifications","summary":"The footage shows specially elected MCA Milka Nyabura Mwangi delivering her words with visible difficulty during county assembly proceedings, prompting criticism that questioned her selection and called the scene embarrassing. Defenders argued that English fluency isn't essential for effective local leadership, pointing out that many leaders use vernacular languages to serve communities well, and Nyandarua Governor Dr. Moses Kiarie Badilisha has backed such nominated MCAs for their grassroots insight. Kenyan law only requires MCAs to read and write in English or Kiswahili, with no degree needed, sparking wider talk on language use and representation in county governance.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:47:34.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108447066401939760"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108212302247854180"},{"post_id":"2108215019259220098"},{"post_id":"2108216920772104617"},{"post_id":"2108325405317042314"},{"post_id":"2108231394535116992"},{"post_id":"2108212302247854180"},{"post_id":"2108215019259220098"},{"post_id":"2108325405317042314"},{"post_id":"2108216920772104617"},{"post_id":"2108231394535116992"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"JD Vance stood before 'FIGHTING VISA FRAUD' banners, spotlighting how Microsoft laid off 6,000 American workers while securing 6,300 H-1B visas.","id":"2108217519312195996","name":"JD Vance Announces Visa Crackdown on Microsoft and Adobe","summary":"At a White House event, Vice President Vance and Labor leaders suspended Microsoft and Adobe from the PERM green card program due to investigations revealing layoffs of Americans alongside heavy use of foreign worker visas. Vance highlighted wage gaps, noting H-1B holders earn $20,000 less than U.S. citizens in similar roles and even less from outsourcing firms, calling it a system of 'indentured servants' undercutting jobs. He defined socialism in America as replacing American workers with foreigners and allowing boys in girls' sports, prompting backlash from critics like Rep. Pramila Jayapal who decried the moves as harmful to legal immigration and innovation.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:10:01.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108217519312195996"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108629711207231517"},{"post_id":"2108648529530867841"},{"post_id":"2108632045614428280"},{"post_id":"2108637361584398832"},{"post_id":"2108639039259852876"},{"post_id":"2108658858486911367"},{"post_id":"2108636618525417612"},{"post_id":"2108638782480142844"},{"post_id":"2108628491105190151"},{"post_id":"2108672663975575722"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108698975104802835","name":"Online Debate Emerges Over Abdulrahman Leme's Character and Political Support for Tinubu's Re-election","summary":"Gimba Kakanda highlighted criticism of Abdulrahman Leme, also known as Madaki, stemming from threats by a self-described mob against supporters of Tinubu's second term candidacy. Supporters defended Leme's longstanding networks, generosity, and mobilization efforts in northern Nigerian politics, predating his public office. The discussion centers on accusations of transactional politics countered by praise for his offline contributions and resilience against critics.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T23:58:34.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108698975104802835"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108474546219040870"},{"post_id":"2108452588668481728"},{"post_id":"2108511720100790349"},{"post_id":"2108447892599914793"},{"post_id":"2108410124343845118"},{"post_id":"2108458892556742894"},{"post_id":"2108468065989984416"},{"post_id":"2108491518159765634"},{"post_id":"2108468201768301041"},{"post_id":"2108480073569566966"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108503175426957453","name":"Nigerian Man Who Voted for President Bola Tinubu Laments Losing Cars and Apartment Due to Economic Hardship","summary":"A Nigerian man who voted for President Bola Tinubu in 2023 expresses regret over his economic situation, stating he has not eaten since morning and faces eviction from his apartment due to unaffordable rent. He claims he owned two cars and lived comfortably before but now struggles severely amid economic hardship.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:58:59.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108503175426957453"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108588029321638189"},{"post_id":"2108579471418867800"},{"post_id":"2108591899217150394"},{"post_id":"2108577716731883642"},{"post_id":"2108607417680584768"},{"post_id":"2108600452917187005"},{"post_id":"2108576925056987227"},{"post_id":"2108579911036481606"},{"post_id":"2108593269638938750"},{"post_id":"2108576455311679916"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Elections"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108618271905939503","name":"Election Commission of India Caps Form 7 Applications by Individual Electors to Curb Bulk Filings","summary":"The Election Commission of India has limited Form 7 applications, used for objecting to names in electoral rolls, to a maximum of 10 per individual elector during the entire claims and objections period and 5 per month during continuous updation of electoral rolls. The measures address complaints of misuse through unsubstantiated bulk filings causing hardship to voters and burdening officials. Electoral Registration Officers are directed to verify applications, conduct hearings, and act against false submissions.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:28:09.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108618271905939503"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108610817939906603"},{"post_id":"2108603882293297645"},{"post_id":"2108681669565988896"},{"post_id":"2108607203422650380"},{"post_id":"2108702324554391728"},{"post_id":"2108664715169661079"},{"post_id":"2108644818280689820"},{"post_id":"2108641981694148847"},{"post_id":"2108618623178940650"},{"post_id":"2108609296451964971"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108649978898059535","name":"Photos emerge of Democratic congressional candidate wearing leather harness and dog collar in BDSM context","summary":"Private photos surfaced online showing a Democratic candidate running in a Long Island district dressed in a leather harness and dog collar. The images depict the candidate in a BDSM context.","updated_at":"2026-10-10T00:10:34.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108649978898059535"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108462914382270595"},{"post_id":"2108497712987676778"},{"post_id":"2108610685273768122"},{"post_id":"2108570673987666362"},{"post_id":"2108564479600423124"},{"post_id":"2108614760262430859"},{"post_id":"2108583844161126702"},{"post_id":"2108466905329680502"},{"post_id":"2108550838398717987"},{"post_id":"2108486518994297242"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Relationships"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108503175061970982","name":"Republican Figure Faces Backlash After Stating Stay-at-Home Dad Role Is Easier Than His Previous Job","summary":"A GOP-affiliated man stated that being a stay-at-home dad was easier than his prior job. The comment prompted a TikTok series by a childless woman targeting him. The statement sparked online debate about the challenges of stay-at-home parenting.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:28:20.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108503175061970982"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108493385858420774"},{"post_id":"2108511752728252896"},{"post_id":"2108528213966356652"},{"post_id":"2108492022067958196"},{"post_id":"2108606179962442208"},{"post_id":"2108545186871845178"},{"post_id":"2108476539616793048"},{"post_id":"2108557373174620605"},{"post_id":"2108572821723205647"},{"post_id":"2108567037509554301"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108607737315655698","name":"Rahul Gandhi and Congress Party Pledge to End Crony Capitalism and Promote Level Playing Field for Businesses in India","summary":"Rahul Gandhi and the Congress party pledged to end crony capitalism in India and create a level playing field for businesses. They committed to building an economy driven by innovation, merit, and hard work rather than political patronage.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T19:31:16.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108607737315655698"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107902590763540577"},{"post_id":"2108229726875603067"},{"post_id":"2108249326883569788"},{"post_id":"2107901312125817156"},{"post_id":"2108216318206120355"},{"post_id":"2108249326883569788"},{"post_id":"2108229726875603067"},{"post_id":"2107828739757510713"},{"post_id":"2108192846213693460"},{"post_id":"2107901312125817156"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Chris Gallant, a National Guard pilot running for Congress, saw old fetish modeling photos resurface. Instead of hiding, he owned them with a bold quip: he makes Christian Grey look like amateur hour.","id":"2107937876327731471","name":"Chris Gallant Embraces Kinky Past Photos in Congressional Race","summary":"The 37-year-old Democratic candidate from New York's First Congressional District modeled leather gear around 2010 for a San Francisco brand, a private shoot when he was under 21. After the New York Post published the images in September, Gallant called it a political attack but leaned in, posting campaign slogans like 'Make Politics Sexy Again' and highlighting his service as a Black Hawk pilot, air traffic controller, and firefighter. Facing Republican incumbent Nick LaLota in a competitive race, his unapologetic stance has drawn mixed online reactions, from praise to questions about his fit for office, keeping his name buzzing ahead of November.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:29:41.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107937876327731471"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107762608870736109"},{"post_id":"2107737376277635454"},{"post_id":"2108106401381802423"},{"post_id":"2108080201716666506"},{"post_id":"2108207201215185311"},{"post_id":"2107762608870736109"},{"post_id":"2107737376277635454"},{"post_id":"2108106401381802423"},{"post_id":"2108150866217718177"},{"post_id":"2108080201716666506"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"One supporter apologized for voting against Tinubu in 2023, now praising fuel subsidy removal and shorter university strikes after seeing reforms take hold.","id":"2107741881522176246","name":"Northern Nigerians Voice Growing Support for Tinubu's 2027 Re-election","summary":"Public posts from Northern Nigeria show a wave of backing for President Bola Ahmed Tinubu's 2027 re-election bid, with users citing policy wins like stabilized Naira, NELFUND student aid, cheaper CNG fuel, and security gains. Some stayed up after prayers to wish him success, urging a full '4+4' term to let tough reforms deliver long-term benefits. Groups like Arewa for Asiwaju mobilize across 19 states, highlighting infrastructure and education projects, even as opposition pushes back on performance over regional turns.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:36:47.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107741881522176246"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108584307279176120"},