iro to tackle deep divisions before casting votes.","id":"2108191090885222866","name":"Palestinian Authority Poised to Postpone Elections After Two Decades","summary":"Mahmoud Abbas and Palestinian groups including Fatah, Hamas, and others are reportedly set to delay the November 28 legislative elections—the first in two decades—to prioritize national dialogue. Sources cite logistical hurdles in Gaza and East Jerusalem, plus internal feuds, with agreements from meetings in Cairo pointing to a possible one-year postponement. Fatah wants elections but insists on consensus, while no official confirmation has come from the Palestinian Authority, and the matter heads to the PLO executive committee.","updated_at":"2026-10-08T15:10:47.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108191090885222866"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108396138890178593"},{"post_id":"2108406635362222570"},{"post_id":"2108398236004192413"},{"post_id":"2108393248087511517"},{"post_id":"2108432488301244793"},{"post_id":"2108407176385454182"},{"post_id":"2108422160683258347"},{"post_id":"2108382490498932800"},{"post_id":"2108378895632204098"},{"post_id":"2108400063516934234"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News","Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Ordinary Ugandans are sharing stories of graft online, fueling a government crackdown that's already led to hundreds of arrests and billions in questioned funds.","id":"2108451351566909900","name":"Ugandans Rally Against Corruption with #ExposeTheCorrupt Campaign","summary":"The #ExposeTheCorrupt push on X supports the State House Anti-Corruption Unit's efforts, resulting in 267 arrests, 253 officials sidelined, and nearly 40 court cases, with Shs22.7 billion under scrutiny across regions. Brig. Gen. Henry Isoke credits citizen tips for exposing service delivery flaws in areas like procurement, education, and health. Users stress how co